==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Condemned Peng]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Aku Doge]] spawns as the boss.
**6 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**8 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**3 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**3 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is optimized for level 18 units. If you struggle, it may be worth waiting for earlier stages to become available and clearing those first.

To clear this stage, you need nothing more than [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]. Start by stalling and having only a single Crazed Dragon take care of the damage, then summon Bahamut and spam everything once the first Condemned Peng is dead. As long as all the attacks are few and powerful, the Brollows will die quickly and only push little, leading to the enemies being unable to advance. You can, of course, add on to the minimum requirements, but it is ill-advised to add low damage cats who rely on attack rate or other things to be good, especially bad units to bring include [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]].

